@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "AFTER INSERT Trigger";
}

<div class="container-fluid py-4">

    <!-- =========================
         PAGE HEADER
    ========================== -->

    <div class="mb-4">

        <h1 class="fw-bold text-primary">
            AFTER INSERT Trigger
        </h1>

        <p class="text-muted fs-5">
            Learn how to create and use an AFTER INSERT Trigger in SQL Server.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         INTRODUCTION
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                What is an AFTER INSERT Trigger?
            </h2>

            <p>
                An <strong>AFTER INSERT Trigger</strong> is a special type of
                SQL Server trigger that automatically executes after a new
                record is successfully inserted into a table.
            </p>

            <p>
                It is commonly used for auditing, logging, maintaining
                related data and performing automatic actions after an
                INSERT operation.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         HOW AFTER INSERT TRIGGER WORKS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                How AFTER INSERT Trigger Works
            </h2>

            <p>
                When an INSERT statement is executed, SQL Server first
                inserts the new record into the table.
            </p>

            <p>
                After the INSERT operation is completed successfully,
                the AFTER INSERT Trigger automatically executes.
            </p>

            <div class="alert alert-info">

                <strong>Flow:</strong>

                <br />

                INSERT Operation
                &nbsp; → &nbsp;
                Record Inserted
                &nbsp; → &nbsp;
                AFTER INSERT Trigger Executes

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         INSERTED TABLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                The INSERTED Table
            </h2>

            <p>
                SQL Server provides a special logical table called
                <strong>inserted</strong> inside an INSERT Trigger.
            </p>

            <p>
                The <strong>inserted</strong> table contains the newly
                inserted records.
            </p>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">

                <strong>Important:</strong>

                The <strong>inserted</strong> table can be used inside
                the trigger to access the newly inserted values.

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         EXAMPLE TABLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Example: Students Table
            </h2>

            <p>
                Let's create a simple Students table for understanding
                the AFTER INSERT Trigger.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE TABLE Students
(
    StudentId INT PRIMARY KEY,
    StudentName VARCHAR(100),
    City VARCHAR(50),
    Age INT
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         AUDIT TABLE
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Create an Audit Table
            </h2>

            <p>
                We can create another table to store information about
                newly inserted students.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE TABLE StudentAudit
(
    AuditId INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY,
    StudentId INT,
    StudentName VARCHAR(100),
    ActionDate DATETIME
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         CREATE AFTER INSERT TRIGGER
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Creating an AFTER INSERT Trigger
            </h2>

            <p>
                Now we will create a trigger that automatically stores
                information in the StudentAudit table whenever a new
                student is inserted.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE TRIGGER trg_AfterInsertStudent
ON Students
AFTER INSERT
AS
BEGIN

    INSERT INTO StudentAudit
    (
        StudentId,
        StudentName,
        ActionDate
    )
    SELECT
        StudentId,
        StudentName,
        GETDATE()
    FROM inserted;

END;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         EXPLANATION
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Explanation
            </h2>

            <div class="table-responsive">

                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                    <thead class="table-primary">

                        <tr>
                            <th>Statement</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                        </tr>

                    </thead>

                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>CREATE TRIGGER</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Creates a new trigger.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>ON Students</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Specifies the table on which the trigger
                                is created.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>AFTER INSERT</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Specifies that the trigger executes
                                after an INSERT operation.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>inserted</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Contains the newly inserted records.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>GETDATE()</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Returns the current date and time.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>

                </table>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         INSERT RECORD
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Insert a New Student
            </h2>

            <p>
                Now insert a new student into the Students table.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>INSERT INTO Students
(
    StudentId,
    StudentName,
    City,
    Age
)
VALUES
(
    101,
    'Rahul',
    'Pune',
    22
);</code></pre>

            <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">

                <strong>What happens?</strong>

                <br />

                The student is inserted into the
                <strong>Students</strong> table.

                <br />

                After the INSERT operation,
                <strong>trg_AfterInsertStudent</strong>
                automatically executes.

                <br />

                The student's details are then stored in the
                <strong>StudentAudit</strong> table.

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         CHECK AUDIT DATA
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Check the Audit Table
            </h2>

            <p>
                Execute the following query to check the data inserted
                by the trigger.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>SELECT *
FROM StudentAudit;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         MULTIPLE INSERTS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                AFTER INSERT Trigger with Multiple Rows
            </h2>

            <p>
                The <strong>inserted</strong> table can contain multiple
                rows when multiple records are inserted at once.
            </p>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>INSERT INTO Students
(
    StudentId,
    StudentName,
    City,
    Age
)
VALUES
(102, 'Priya', 'Mumbai', 23),
(103, 'Amit', 'Pune', 24),
(104, 'Sneha', 'Nashik', 22);</code></pre>

            <p class="mt-3">
                The trigger executes once for the INSERT statement and
                processes the rows available in the
                <strong>inserted</strong> table.
            </p>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         IMPORTANT POINTS
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Important Points
            </h2>

            <ul>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    AFTER INSERT Trigger executes after an INSERT operation.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    It is automatically executed by SQL Server.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    The <strong>inserted</strong> logical table contains
                    newly inserted rows.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    A trigger can be used for auditing and logging.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    A trigger should be designed carefully because it
                    executes automatically.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Triggers can process multiple inserted rows.
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SYNTAX
    ========================== -->

    <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">

        <div class="card-body">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                AFTER INSERT Trigger Syntax
            </h2>

            <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>CREATE TRIGGER TriggerName
ON TableName
AFTER INSERT
AS
BEGIN

    -- Trigger statements

END;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- =========================
         SUMMARY
    ========================== -->

    <div class="alert alert-primary shadow-sm mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Summary
        </h2>

        <p class="mb-2">
            An <strong>AFTER INSERT Trigger</strong> automatically
            executes after a successful INSERT operation.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-2">
            It is useful for auditing, logging and performing
            automatic operations after new records are inserted.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-0">
            The <strong>inserted</strong> logical table provides access
            to the newly inserted records inside the trigger.
        </p>

    </div>


